`timeout-minutes: 45` was set on this job in da5e1ee0, when the leg was written, as a guess
and never checked against a run. The measured macOS leg -- same crates, same cache key, an
arm64 runner that is the faster of the two -- finishes in 31m17s. Windows spent its entire
budget inside the test step, so this leg has now produced three consecutive shapes of "no
Windows result": a parse failure (step 3), a build failure (step 9, ~80 s), and a cap hit
(step 9, 45m15s). The first two were fixed in earlier sections; the third is the cap, and a
leg that always dies at the cap is indistinguishable from a leg that was deleted. Raised to
75 minutes in this commit, with the two measurements written above the setting.

This is still not evidence that the Windows tests pass. It is evidence about *why* they
have never reported, and the next push is the first one in which the step is expected to
reach a verdict.

