            grok_build::grep::ripgrep, grok_build::enter_plan_mode, gitignore::tests

== 5c. Structural changes so a hang can never again erase five crates' verdicts

`cargo test --locked --no-fail-fast -p ... -p xai-grok-tools` ran all six target-OS crates in
one step, so one stuck test in the largest crate consumed the remaining budget *and* the
`test result:` summary of everything already compiled. The step is now split in
`.github/workflows/ci.yml` into `cargo test (target-OS crates: except xai-grok-tools)` and
`cargo test (target-OS crates: xai-grok-tools)`, each `timeout-minutes: 35` with `if:
always()` on the second, inside the job's 75-minute budget. A hang in `xai-grok-tools` can
now cost that crate its own verdict and nothing else.

Two guards came out of authoring that split:

* `scripts/ci/check-workflow-yaml.py` -- the new step names contain `": "`, and unquoted that
  is a YAML mapping separator: PyYAML refused the file at line 293, which would have meant a
  workflow that parses to nothing and runs **no jobs at all**. `check-workflow-shells.py` and
  `check-workflow-toolchain.py` both reported OK on the broken file, because both extract
  `run:` blocks with a regex and never ask whether the document is a valid mapping. The new
  guard tracks block-scalar state, strips comments the way YAML does, and flags a `": "` in a
  plain scalar; its self-tests cross-check every fixture against `yaml.safe_load`.
* `scripts/ci/check-spawn-cwd-portability.py` -- the guard that now fails a `-p xai-grok-tools`
  test whose `cwd`/`working_directory`/`.current_dir()` is a POSIX-absolute path under a root
  no Windows host has. Extending it to the `cwd:` field (the `TaskToolInput` form) is what
  would have caught this class the first time. It reads the crate list by unioning every
  `cargo test (target-OS crates: ...)` step, so the split above cannot silently drop a crate
  out of its scan, and it fails closed if a `cargo test -p` step exists on the platform job
  that the step-name prefix does not cover.

Both are wired into `.github/workflows/ci.yml` (`workflows-present`) and
`scripts/verify-in-docker.sh`, and `check-guard-wiring.py` enforces that pairing.

