== 5e. What section 5 is still not evidence about

* No Windows machine was used. Every Windows number above is read out of the log of a run
  another machine executed; the mutation proof in 5a was run on Linux against the same
  production branch. Whether the fixes make the Windows leg green is answered by the next
  push, not by this file.
* The 67 failures left after the two fixed groups (124 − 54 terminal − 3 task) have no
  assertion text in this
  run and no stated cause. They are listed so the next Windows log can be diffed against a
  known set, not because they are understood. The `test_kill_returns_signal` and
  `corrupt_config_never_changes_update_outcome` failures quoted in 5b are not part of the 124
  -- they come from the `xai-grok-shell-terminal` and `xai-grok-pager-bin` binaries.
* The "one stuck test erases the whole binary's summary" mechanism is inferred from libtest's
  documented printing order plus the observed absence of a summary line; I did not reproduce
  a hung libtest run to watch it happen.
* Whether 35 + 35 minutes is enough for the two split steps on Windows: the 25m43s of that
  45m15s was compilation, which is shared and cached, so the split estimate applies to the
  test phase only. This is an estimate, and the split makes the next measurement readable
  either way.

